  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EU Support to democracy, peace and social cohesion in Sierra Leone</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In view of the local, parliamentary and presidential elections forecast in 2023, high political polarisation and a culture of confrontational engagement between political parties, the European Union renews its commitment towards democratic governance in Sierra Leone to support the conduct of peaceful and credible elections and enhance citizens&#xbf; (especially women and youth) participation in electoral processes and political space.The present action aims at consolidating the democratic process in Sierra Leone and at inspiring and supporting change processes undertaken by the National Electoral Commission, Political Parties Registration Commission, Judiciary, Sierra Leone Police and promote rights holders and citizens participation (notably women, girls and youth) in democratic governance and&amp;nbsp;political process through strengthening of CSO-led initiatives, media and democratic institutions (Parliament) supporting transparency and accountability of duty bearers.</narrative>
  </description>
